course: dictionary
lesson: 9812
title: Swathe: a strip, a wrap, a big part
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one to use. «Swathe» can be a noun (a thing) or a verb (an action). Read the words around it first.
explain: In «Sleep takes him as a swathe of barley is folded into the arms of the reaping machine», the clues are barley and reaping machine. Barley is a crop, and a machine is cutting it down, so a swathe here is a long, wide strip of crop.
explain: Now try the other meanings. A hurt person is «swathed in bandages» and a baby is «swathed in blankets», so swathe can also mean to wrap something up. When you read «a swathe of the country», a big part of the land is meant. Ask: which meaning fits the sentence?
fact: A swathe is a long, wide strip or area of land, crops or something else.
fact: To swathe something is to wrap it up in cloth or bandages.
fact: «A swathe of the country» means a large part of the country.
fact: When grass or corn is cut with a scythe, each cut row is a swathe.
fact: «Cut a swathe through» means to move through and knock things down.
exercise: «Sleep takes him as a swathe of barley is folded into the arms of the reaping machine.» What is a swathe here? | A small bird | A bandage round a sore finger | A type of machine | *A long, wide strip of crop
exercise: «The nurse swathed the boy's arm in clean white bandages.» What does swathed mean? | *Wrapped up | Painted bright red | Cut into pieces | Dropped on the floor
exercise: «The forest covers a swathe of the north.» What does swathe mean here? | A sudden storm | A kind of boat | *A large part | A small hut
test: «The mower cut a swathe through the long grass.» What does cut a swathe through mean? | *Moved through and knocked things down | Counted every blade of grass | Stopped to rest in the shade | Watered the grass slowly
test: «The baby was swathed in a soft blue blanket.» What does swathed mean? | *Wrapped up | Lost in the house | Woken up suddenly | Painted with stripes
exam: «A swathe of the field was cut and left in neat rows.» What does swathe mean here? | A kind of shoe | *A long, wide strip of crop | A bandage for a broken leg | A loud noise
